WEBVTT

00:03.490 --> 00:05.310
For it to have become like this...

00:05.310 --> 00:06.190
Eh?

00:06.190 --> 00:09.690
But you requested that the clock be restored to its original state...

00:09.690 --> 00:13.750
Well that's true... my way of asking was bad.

00:14.760 --> 00:15.950
Umm...

00:15.950 --> 00:17.910
I fixed what was broken.

00:17.910 --> 00:20.360
And I made it look brand-new as well.

00:21.080 --> 00:23.990
If that was case I could have asked a watch dealer!

00:25.220 --> 00:26.080
Umm...

00:26.080 --> 00:30.460
I'm sorry, but could you tell us a bit more about the details?

00:30.460 --> 00:31.540
Yeah...

00:34.130 --> 00:38.180
When my master gave me this watch,

00:38.180 --> 00:41.470
my name was written here.

00:41.470 --> 00:42.420
Your name?

00:43.290 --> 00:46.440
I was really happy when I got it.

00:47.230 --> 00:51.280
But after wearing it for a while, it became dirty.

00:52.550 --> 00:54.070
I wanted to polish it,

00:54.070 --> 00:57.410
but then the characters would be erased as well, right?

00:57.410 --> 00:58.220
Yes.

00:58.750 --> 01:03.140
These days, I wanted to read what my master wrote.

01:03.860 --> 01:08.290
That's why I requested to have it restored back to the way it was.

01:08.990 --> 01:14.420
Then I could once again see his writing.

01:14.420 --> 01:16.010
Then you should have-

01:16.010 --> 01:21.870
You're right, if I had explained it properly, this wouldn't have happened.

01:22.510 --> 01:23.230
I...

01:22.510 --> 01:25.310
We're really sorry about this.

01:25.310 --> 01:27.020
It's his fault.

01:27.020 --> 01:29.400
After all, he is just a trainee.

01:29.400 --> 01:31.930
Perhaps if he asked more...

01:31.440 --> 01:32.740
I failed?

01:33.290 --> 01:34.440
But I did-

01:34.440 --> 01:36.030
Come on, Kuroda! Just apologize!

01:38.370 --> 01:39.940
My apologies.

01:44.060 --> 01:45.200
Hey, stop goofing around.

01:45.200 --> 01:46.700
Can't you be more serious?

01:47.480 --> 01:49.500
I'm not really goofing around.

01:49.500 --> 01:54.300
You know, I wonder if you even pay attention when people are speaking.

01:54.300 --> 01:55.130
Umm...

01:55.130 --> 01:56.470
I am trying to listen.

01:57.180 --> 01:58.680
Just trying won't do it.

01:59.420 --> 02:02.050
And you were acting all arrogant going, "sure, sure".

02:02.400 --> 02:04.740
But you can't do it with your magic at all.

02:09.120 --> 02:10.650
You can stop now.

02:10.650 --> 02:14.020
Let the pro over there do it, she's a "real" mage.

02:14.020 --> 02:15.980
But the trainee...

02:15.980 --> 02:17.570
He just won't do.

02:17.570 --> 02:20.340
Can't you just do it quickly?

02:22.240 --> 02:25.960
You know, shouldn't you study some more magic first?

02:26.520 --> 02:29.330
I'm very sorry, then let me...

02:29.330 --> 02:31.540
That's right, hurry up and do it.

02:31.540 --> 02:32.110
Dam...

02:32.110 --> 02:32.840
Okay.

04:24.670 --> 04:28.700
Geez, I wanted to take a better look at those sandals.

04:28.700 --> 04:30.040
I'm sorry.

04:30.040 --> 04:32.580
I'm satisfied that I got these hair clips.

04:32.580 --> 04:34.920
It goes well with the Yukata from last time.

04:34.920 --> 04:35.560
Yeah!

04:36.710 --> 04:38.340
Ah, excuse me.

04:39.540 --> 04:40.830
Yes, that's fine.

04:39.960 --> 04:42.090
Ruriko-chan is an interesting girl.

04:42.090 --> 04:43.570
Yeah, I'm not really busy at the moment.

04:42.820 --> 04:45.260
She tricked the three of us.

04:44.550 --> 04:45.260
Huh?

04:45.940 --> 04:47.490
I'm in Shimokitazawa right now.

04:48.210 --> 04:49.870
I'm not sure.

04:50.750 --> 04:54.030
Sure, then at 7pm in front of the station.

04:54.660 --> 04:55.380
Later.

04:56.900 --> 04:58.230
Yamabuki Hiyori!

04:58.230 --> 05:00.070
Come, let's go!

05:00.070 --> 05:02.320
Then Sora-chan, see you tomorrow!

05:03.840 --> 05:06.720
Sora-chan, see you tomorrow!

05:11.050 --> 05:12.240
Thanks for waiting.

05:12.240 --> 05:13.070
Huh?

05:13.560 --> 05:14.500
Yeah.

05:14.500 --> 05:16.580
So, what's the matter?

05:17.220 --> 05:19.850
Asagi, have you heard of Nakano Broadway?

05:20.550 --> 05:21.390
I haven't.

05:22.620 --> 05:23.670
What is that?

05:26.410 --> 05:30.290
I wanted to come here with you.

05:30.650 --> 05:31.640
Why is that?

05:31.640 --> 05:34.730
I wanted to see what your reaction was.

05:35.620 --> 05:36.670
Curiosity, eh?

05:38.560 --> 05:44.030
This place has a lot of interesting things for both adults and children.

05:44.030 --> 05:45.510
It's a strange place.

05:46.270 --> 05:49.190
It's surprising that you are an Akiba-fanatic, Kuroda Kouji.

05:49.780 --> 05:51.070
An Akiba-fanatic...

05:52.840 --> 05:56.910
Nakano Broadway was constructed in 1966.

05:56.910 --> 06:00.170
For over 40 years, it's been a shopping complex.

06:00.170 --> 06:00.960
Oh?

06:00.960 --> 06:03.090
It's a Kuroda Kouji-like introduction.

06:04.120 --> 06:07.590
From the basement to 4th floor is all commerce.

06:07.590 --> 06:10.030
The 5th through 10th floors are expensive residences.

06:10.790 --> 06:15.310
Back in the 70s, Aoshima Yukio and Kenji Sawada were living here.

06:15.310 --> 06:17.120
Ijiwaru Baasan and Julie?

06:15.310 --> 06:18.730
Ijiwaru Baasan (いじわるばあさん - A Tricky Grandmother) one of Aoshima's TV appearances.
Julie (ジュリー) is Sawada Kenji's nickname.

06:17.680 --> 06:18.730
Asagi...

06:32.740 --> 06:33.620
Oh!

06:33.620 --> 06:35.980
It's the red fragment deluxe version!

06:36.790 --> 06:38.580
Shall I try it?

06:40.120 --> 06:42.450
I can't believe they have this book.

06:43.150 --> 06:45.500
"Ugly women are better off dead"?

06:45.500 --> 06:46.870
That's a bit harsh.

06:47.610 --> 06:49.090
Ah, it's Maruo!

06:49.090 --> 06:50.510
Should I buy it?

06:50.510 --> 06:53.730
This place's Kanba-che is pretty interesting.

06:55.300 --> 06:56.680
Do you know about P-Model?

06:56.680 --> 06:57.750
Not at all.

06:58.460 --> 07:00.810
Do you listen to that, Kuroda Kouji?

07:00.810 --> 07:01.590
Yeah.

07:01.980 --> 07:03.510
You're just like Hiyo-chan.

07:04.010 --> 07:05.640
What does Yamabuki listen to?

07:06.440 --> 07:08.490
English New Wave.

07:09.070 --> 07:11.800
She also mentioned New Order and Echo and the Bunnymen.

07:15.700 --> 07:17.950
You can feel the ups and downs of life.

07:17.950 --> 07:20.750
Recently, many shops have had to close.

07:22.310 --> 07:24.900
But it was fun to visit this place with you.

07:25.490 --> 07:27.020
It was fun for me too.

07:31.330 --> 07:35.470
Then, what was it that Kuroda Kouji wanted to tell me?

07:36.930 --> 07:40.140
Don't you feel unsatisfied with your magical training?

07:40.140 --> 07:40.890
Huh?

07:41.450 --> 07:45.100
It's always just some small-scale, simple magic.

07:45.100 --> 07:46.070
Really?

07:46.530 --> 07:48.440
Lots of selfish clients.

07:48.440 --> 07:51.290
Even if I follow their request, they still complain.

07:52.800 --> 07:56.020
Those people... what do they know about magic...

07:56.810 --> 07:58.080
What are you trying to say?

07:58.080 --> 07:58.810
Huh?

08:00.190 --> 08:03.050
I mean, magic on a much bigger scale...

08:02.320 --> 08:05.020
If it's a question I hear, I'll give you an answer.

08:05.740 --> 08:09.300
However, I will not listen to your boring and arrogant complaints.

08:13.810 --> 08:16.590
Kuroda Kouji, wait up!

08:16.590 --> 08:17.800
Wait up!

08:17.800 --> 08:18.570
Stop!

08:19.880 --> 08:24.130
Are you saying that stuff was the reason you called me all the way out here?

08:25.200 --> 08:26.680
"That stuff"?

08:27.470 --> 08:31.440
Whether it's small or big, it's still magic.

08:32.470 --> 08:33.610
Is that so?

08:33.610 --> 08:36.820
Besides, looking down on your clients...

08:36.820 --> 08:38.710
Just who the hell do you think you are?

08:40.590 --> 08:42.120
You're always like that.

08:42.120 --> 08:42.920
Oh?

08:43.570 --> 08:45.420
You don't care about how others feel.

08:45.980 --> 08:47.120
What's that supposed to mean?

08:47.610 --> 08:52.730
I do care about my own feelings, but I also respect the feelings of others.

08:53.760 --> 08:54.580
Then...

08:55.660 --> 08:56.680
what about mine?

08:56.680 --> 08:59.210
I don't want to hear your complaints.

09:02.130 --> 09:03.240
Asagi.

09:11.040 --> 09:12.980
Sayori-chan, another bowl please.

09:12.980 --> 09:14.420
It's Sayori-obasan!

09:16.990 --> 09:18.230
What is it?

09:20.830 --> 09:22.820
Don't check your mail during a meal.

09:24.260 --> 09:25.070
Gouta-kun!

09:27.880 --> 09:28.980
It's from Kuroda.

09:29.900 --> 09:31.090
Kuroda?

09:31.090 --> 09:32.060
Another trainee?

09:34.670 --> 09:35.550
That guy said...

09:35.550 --> 09:36.740
he's quitting.

09:37.150 --> 09:38.130
Huh?

09:38.760 --> 09:40.750
Is he serious?

09:41.450 --> 09:42.420
Seems so.

09:51.150 --> 09:54.490
Kuroda-kun always seemed to have confidence in himself though...

09:55.510 --> 09:58.150
Suzuki, have you ever thought about going home?

09:58.150 --> 09:59.010
Huh?

09:59.550 --> 10:00.990
To Hokkaido?

10:01.490 --> 10:03.660
I've thought about it many times.

10:03.660 --> 10:05.020
I...

10:05.890 --> 10:09.590
About magic, our responsibility for the clients is heavy, right?

10:11.370 --> 10:14.750
That's why I think that every trainee is a bit worried.

10:15.980 --> 10:17.220
That's true.

10:21.940 --> 10:25.560
But when they thank us, it's the best!

10:26.200 --> 10:26.960
Yeah.

10:29.100 --> 10:31.480
Gouta-kun, you've changed.

10:31.480 --> 10:32.290
Huh?

10:32.680 --> 10:33.940
You're like an adult.

10:33.940 --> 10:35.190
What do you mean by that?

11:24.560 --> 11:28.660
When I got the mail from Hono-chan, I was really shocked...

11:28.660 --> 11:31.120
You seem to be on good terms with Kuroda-kun.

11:31.700 --> 11:35.000
We didn't send mail until recently.

11:35.000 --> 11:37.050
What happened to Kuroda?

11:38.100 --> 11:41.160
An instructor caught him as he was trying to run home.

11:41.650 --> 11:43.380
He's still being observed.

11:44.220 --> 11:48.090
And I always thought it was easy for him.

11:49.700 --> 11:54.650
Those strong and conceited types show their unexpected weak spots when they falter.

11:55.460 --> 11:56.610
Aren't you like that too, Hono-chan?

11:56.610 --> 11:58.920
I mean in general.

12:00.730 --> 12:03.630
People who quit over small issues...

12:04.690 --> 12:06.120
I can't forgive them.

12:06.120 --> 12:08.410
Let's go see Kuroda-kun.

12:08.410 --> 12:09.490
Yeah!

12:10.020 --> 12:11.700
I'm not going.

12:11.700 --> 12:13.000
Why?

12:13.000 --> 12:14.590
It's a waste of time.

12:26.100 --> 12:28.460
So, let's meet at 7pm at Nakano Station.

12:29.890 --> 12:32.300
Hono-chan really won't come with us?

12:36.540 --> 12:38.030
Okay, let's do it that way.

12:38.640 --> 12:41.440
Well then, do your best on today's practice too!

12:41.440 --> 12:42.260
Yes!

12:45.340 --> 12:47.820
Fune-sama, get me one will you?

12:47.820 --> 12:48.910
All right.

12:48.910 --> 12:50.220
How about you, Sora-chan?

12:50.530 --> 12:52.040
I'm fine.

12:52.620 --> 12:54.370
It looks like it will be a hot day.

12:54.370 --> 12:55.420
Yes, it does.

12:57.170 --> 12:57.930
Delicious!

13:00.820 --> 13:02.590
Sora-chan, sorry to keep you waiting.

13:03.130 --> 13:04.850
Huh, Sora-chan?

13:08.820 --> 13:11.010
Geez, so noisy.

13:14.370 --> 13:15.940
Sorry to keep you waiting...

13:16.380 --> 13:17.810
Sora...chan?

13:18.850 --> 13:20.770
Sora-chan, are you okay?

13:20.770 --> 13:21.820
Get ahold of yourself!

13:21.820 --> 13:23.070
I'll go call an ambulance right away.

13:23.070 --> 13:25.750
I'm okay, so...

13:26.450 --> 13:28.180
Don't call the ambulance.

13:28.760 --> 13:29.540
But...

13:30.070 --> 13:32.140
Get ahold of yourself, Sora-chan!

13:31.700 --> 13:33.890
Sora-chan, what's wrong?

13:34.360 --> 13:35.440
Teacher!

13:43.340 --> 13:45.050
Suzuki has a cold?

13:45.640 --> 13:47.260
She really didn't seem to, though.

13:47.920 --> 13:50.290
She probably overworked herself until now.

13:51.510 --> 13:53.680
If she didn't feel well, she should have told us...

13:53.680 --> 13:57.520
She must have given it a lot of thought and just decided to endure it.

13:59.440 --> 14:02.290
Is it really all right not to bring her to the hospital?

14:03.110 --> 14:05.980
I will take her to the hospital if her fever doesn't subside.

14:07.760 --> 14:10.600
Should we contact her mother in Hokkaido?

14:18.130 --> 14:19.860
Sora-chan must have it rough.

14:21.050 --> 14:23.670
I feel somewhat left out.

14:25.160 --> 14:28.210
You know, a girl has many things to think about. It's not easy.

14:33.410 --> 14:35.970
Suzuki told me about these goldfish.

14:35.970 --> 14:37.890
It would be nice if she could visit us occasionally.

14:38.360 --> 14:40.850
Her daughter has a strong personality.

14:40.850 --> 14:42.010
Are they alike?

14:42.460 --> 14:43.950
They look completely different.

14:44.730 --> 14:46.510
But their personalities are identical.

14:49.710 --> 14:52.080
I heard that one student has given up on the training?

14:52.560 --> 14:54.020
His name is Kuroda.

14:54.490 --> 14:55.630
A guy.

14:56.570 --> 14:58.860
But I hope you won't be too harsh with him.

15:00.030 --> 15:03.160
You see, life is long.

15:04.430 --> 15:07.640
Even if I go over to Kuroda's place, there might not be much I can do.

15:08.590 --> 15:10.840
Just seeing him should be enough.

15:14.320 --> 15:15.180
Huh?

15:15.180 --> 15:16.720
You're by yourself today?

15:16.720 --> 15:17.640
Ah?

15:17.640 --> 15:18.770
You mean me?

15:18.770 --> 15:22.270
Yeah, where is the girl with long hair who's always with you?

15:22.270 --> 15:24.860
Ah, she has a cold.

15:25.510 --> 15:26.450
I see.

15:31.200 --> 15:32.480
Good evening, everybody.

15:34.460 --> 15:37.080
My name is Yasuko, and I'm always singing here.

15:38.920 --> 15:42.870
Let's see...  I will sing an original song today.

15:42.870 --> 15:43.710
Sounds good.

15:43.710 --> 15:44.630
We want to hear it.

15:46.220 --> 15:48.460
Then... "Temporary Things".

16:44.370 --> 16:45.540
Sorry to keep you waiting.

16:46.400 --> 16:47.560
Huh?

16:47.560 --> 16:49.400
Just you, Midorikawa-kun?

16:49.400 --> 16:52.900
Yes, Suzuki seems to have caught a cold.

16:52.900 --> 16:55.380
Hmm... I see.

16:55.920 --> 16:57.310
Now then, shall we go?

16:57.710 --> 16:58.480
Sure.

17:03.180 --> 17:07.300
I'm sorry for making everyone worry.

17:08.180 --> 17:11.420
I think we should be the one to say sorry for troubling you.

17:11.940 --> 17:13.010
Not at all.

17:13.010 --> 17:15.450
I think that both of you will be able to cheer him up.

17:18.700 --> 17:20.790
I want to think by myself.

17:21.410 --> 17:23.260
Could you please not bother me.

17:24.650 --> 17:25.470
Kuroda?

17:26.390 --> 17:28.010
It's me, Midorikawa.

17:28.540 --> 17:29.420
Midorikawa?

17:30.050 --> 17:32.220
Have you been eating?

17:33.540 --> 17:36.290
You know... maybe I'm not the right person to say this...

17:36.740 --> 17:40.600
Even if the going gets rough now, life is long.

17:41.290 --> 17:43.440
You can quickly get back on track.

17:43.970 --> 17:45.000
I...

17:45.000 --> 17:46.000
Kuroda-kun.

17:46.000 --> 17:48.790
If you really want to quit that badly, then I think you should just do it.

17:48.790 --> 17:50.210
Hey, Yamabuki!

17:50.210 --> 17:54.800
After all, I'm sure you've thought about it a lot and you still think you should quit.

17:56.000 --> 17:58.130
That's not true, I just...

17:58.130 --> 17:59.760
Hey, Kuroda-kun.

17:59.760 --> 18:01.350
Can you come out so we can talk?

18:01.810 --> 18:02.760
That's right.

18:02.760 --> 18:04.840
Kuroda, let us see you.

18:05.730 --> 18:09.810
Kuroda-kun, I will think about how to guide you.

18:11.170 --> 18:15.760
If you really want to quit, I want us to think about it together.

18:18.160 --> 18:19.070
I...

18:27.640 --> 18:28.420
Asagi...

18:28.920 --> 18:29.950
Hono-chan!

18:34.660 --> 18:36.990
Kuroda Kouji, come out!

18:38.020 --> 18:41.030
Unlocking the door is simple for magic users.

18:43.810 --> 18:48.310
Midorikawa Gouta, who's standing right here, is working hard even if he doesn't understand it all!

18:48.990 --> 18:52.150
I would understand it if Midorikawa Gouta was the one who ran away.

18:52.150 --> 18:53.350
Hey, Asagi!

18:53.810 --> 18:57.870
Because no matter how hard he tries, he can't do it, so it can't be helped.

18:59.170 --> 19:05.280
But you, Kuroda Kouji, you haven't put in any effort and you just want to escape from reality.

19:05.280 --> 19:07.910
So I will not sympathize with you.

19:10.270 --> 19:12.040
I don't want to be sympathized.

19:12.040 --> 19:13.330
Face it!

19:14.010 --> 19:17.200
You are a failure in your magic training.

19:17.980 --> 19:19.550
I am not wrong.

19:19.550 --> 19:21.680
You have failed!

19:21.680 --> 19:22.970
Shut up!

19:22.970 --> 19:24.290
No, on the contrary!

19:25.060 --> 19:25.960
Humans...

19:26.580 --> 19:27.910
make mistakes.

19:28.640 --> 19:30.320
They are fallible.

19:33.590 --> 19:36.260
Because humans use magic...

19:36.920 --> 19:38.370
there will be times where they're mistaken.

19:39.240 --> 19:41.690
And the values differ from person to person.

19:42.480 --> 19:45.930
That's why, what's most important is what happens after the mistake.

19:46.510 --> 19:50.560
If you can accept your own failure, hold on to it and continue forward!

19:51.590 --> 19:54.610
If you run away now, you will just keep running away forever.

19:55.640 --> 19:57.970
Kuroda Kouji, is your pride fine with that?

20:00.930 --> 20:03.630
Right now, Suzuki Sora is staying in bed with a cold.

20:03.630 --> 20:04.590
Sora?

20:04.590 --> 20:07.350
That girl, she really gets into other people's business.

20:08.690 --> 20:11.310
Meddling with people's business must be contagious.

20:12.420 --> 20:16.230
Kuroda Kouji, where is the strength that I saw when I first met you?

20:16.820 --> 20:18.570
That was the real you, right?

20:19.830 --> 20:23.490
Fine, close yourself in the room and don't come out.

20:23.490 --> 20:25.460
I can't feel you in there anymore.

20:26.710 --> 20:27.430
Oh,

20:28.240 --> 20:30.100
Hono-chan, wait a second.

20:33.340 --> 20:34.620
Hey, Kuroda!

20:34.620 --> 20:37.600
It seems we can't get a hold of her now...

20:39.340 --> 20:40.000
I...

20:42.000 --> 20:42.830
I...

20:46.640 --> 20:48.300
I knew you would come.

20:48.300 --> 20:50.400
Don't talk about things you don't know.

20:51.170 --> 20:53.790
I was totally moved.

20:59.790 --> 21:00.710
Who are you texting?

21:02.730 --> 21:04.630
I think I better let Suzuki know.

21:05.130 --> 21:06.200
I see,

21:06.670 --> 21:08.910
Midorikawa-kun is very kind.

21:08.910 --> 21:09.950
Me?

21:09.950 --> 21:12.210
"I don't know how to say it well..."

21:12.860 --> 21:13.590
Um...

21:14.150 --> 21:14.960
sent.

21:18.890 --> 21:23.060
It'd be nice if Kuroda would change his mind.

21:26.420 --> 21:28.930
You really are kind.

23:06.780 --> 23:09.190
Have you ever unexpectedly done something,

23:09.190 --> 23:12.340
which you normally wouldn't have been able to do, no matter how hard you've tried?

23:12.960 --> 23:14.620
Next time: Mages

23:15.370 --> 23:17.910
The shining light on the sea is too bright.

23:17.910 --> 23:19.560
It hurts my eyes!
